WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.310
In 2023, the US unemployment
rate averaged just 3.6 percent.

2
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.030
That sounds like nearly
everyone has a job.

3
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.270
But in the same year,

4
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:14.630
only 62.6 percent of adults
were in the labor force.

5
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.550
Back in 2000, that figure
peaked at 67.3 percent.

6
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.830
So who counts as unemployed,

7
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.910
and who slips through the count?

8
00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.730
In this mission, you'll
sort every adult into three

9
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.090
groups and calculate
two key rates yourself.

10
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.870
Then you'll find out which people
the official rate leaves out.

11
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.320
Your mission: find out who
the unemployment rate counts,

12
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.530
and who it misses.
